From 50840caeb6f80ff08af906052222c739fbb788ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Hephaestus (Paperclip)" <hephaestus@gnomon.labs>
Date: Wed, 27 May 2026 11:21:59 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(process-loss): classify infra vs agent cause for process
 loss events (GNO-182)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Implements §4 signal #4 (apiHealthy) and the full four-signal classification
pipeline for process-loss events as specified in GNO-128 §4.

- New `process-loss-recovery.ts`: `classifyProcessLossCause` with four signals
  (inter-agent correlation, clean stderr, exit 137, API healthy) and confidence
  tagging (primary vs weak). `makeApiHealthCache` for zero-latency signal #4.
- `heartbeat.ts`: two-pass reap pre-computes per-company peer lists (signal #1);
  wires `apiHealthy` from the scheduler health cache; persists
  `processLossCauseClass` and `processLossClassifyConfidence` on each reaped run;
  calls `markTick()` at end of successful pass.
- DB: migrations 0092/0093 add `process_loss_cause_class` and
  `process_loss_classify_confidence` columns to `heartbeat_runs`.
- Tests: unit coverage for all four signals, confidence levels, STACK_TRACE_PATTERN
  variants (V8/Python/JVM), and the TTL cache behaviour.

Co-Authored-By: Paperclip <noreply@paperclip.ing>
